    "body": "@xirzec Thanks for raising this issue. It looks like even Firefox doesn't support things like `opacity`, `visibility`, and `display`, and both Chrome and Firefox support padding in the x-axis but not the y-axis.\r\n\r\nMy guess is the best thing for now is to first get a basic list of necessary \"core\" already-widely-supported properties, as those are obviously a priority and fair game for developers to expect to work. As far as an extensive list goes, perhaps @paulirish may have some information regarding what properties Chrome allows/supports? Maybe this could help us curate a core set of properties assuming this is the best route to go.",
